{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "3JN",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The elder to the well-beloved Gaius, whom I love in truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I rejoiced greatly, when the brethren came and testified of the truth that is in thee, even as thou walkest in the truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have no greater joy than to hear that my children walk in truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Beloved, thou doest faithfully whatever thou doest to the brethren, and to strangers;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who have borne testimony of thy charity before the church: whom if thou shalt bring forward on their journey after a godly sort, thou wilt do well:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because for his name's sake they went forth, taking nothing from the Gentiles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We therefore ought to receive such, that we may be fellow-helpers to the truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I wrote to the church: but Diotrephes, who loveth to have the pre-eminence among them, receiveth us not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore, if I come, I will remember his deeds which he doeth, prating against us with malicious words: and not content with that, neither doth he himself receive the brethren, and forbiddeth them that would, and casteth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out of the church.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Beloved, follow not that which is evil, but that which is good. He that doeth good is of God: but he that doeth evil hath not seen God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Demetrius hath good report by all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and by the truth itself: and we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "also",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bear testimony; and ye know that our testimony is true.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I had many things to write, but I will not with ink and pen write to thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3JN.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:3JN.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I trust I shall shortly see thee, and we shall speak face to face. Peace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to thee. ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " friends salute thee. Greet the friends by name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
